---
source: tests/cli_git.rs
expression: help
---
Reflow broken markdown tables

Usage: mdtablefix [OPTIONS] [FILES]...

Arguments:
  [FILES]...  Markdown files to fix

Options:
      --in-place                    Rewrite files in place
      --check                       Report which files would be reformatted, and by how many lines
      --diff                        Print a unified diff for each file that would be reformatted
      --list-files                  Print the selected paths and exit, without reading or writing them
      --git[=<BOOL>]                Select Markdown files tracked by Git beneath the current directory [possible values: true, false]
      --include-untracked[=<BOOL>]  Also select untracked files that Git does not ignore [possible values: true, false]
      --md-exts <EXT>               File extensions to select under `--git` [default: md,mdc,markdown]
      --allow-conflicted[=<BOOL>]   Rewrite files containing conflict markers during a merge or rebase [possible values: true, false]
      --wrap[=<BOOL>]               Wrap paragraphs and list items to 80 columns [possible values: true, false]
      --renumber[=<BOOL>]           Renumber ordered list items [possible values: true, false]
      --breaks[=<BOOL>]             Reformat thematic breaks as underscores [possible values: true, false]
      --ellipsis[=<BOOL>]           Replace "..." with the ellipsis character [possible values: true, false]
      --fences[=<BOOL>]             Normalize fence delimiters to three backticks [possible values: true, false]
      --footnotes[=<BOOL>]          Convert bare numeric references and the final numbered list to Markdown footnote links [possible values: true, false]
      --code-emphasis[=<BOOL>]      Fix emphasis markers adjacent to inline code [possible values: true, false]
      --headings[=<BOOL>]           Convert Setext-style headings to hash-prefixed headings [possible values: true, false]
  -h, --help                        Print help
  -V, --version                     Print version
